To achieve this, you'll need to make some modifications to your Nginx configuration and your website's HTML structure.

Modified Nginx Configuration:

You'll need to add a variable to store the post ID and then use that variable to generate the link. You can add the following lines to your existing `server` block:
```nginx
server {
    listen 443 ssl http2;
    listen [::]:443 ssl http2;
    server_name www.askfundu.com;
    root /usr/share/nginx/html;

    # ... (rest of the configuration remains the same)

    location / {
        root /usr/share/nginx/html;
        index index.html index.htm;
        try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;

        # Add a variable to store the post ID
        set $post_id 0;

        # Loop through all files in the HTML directory
        if ($uri ~* "^/([^.]+)\.html$") {
            set $post_id $1;
        }
    }

    # ... (rest of the configuration remains the same)
}
```
This sets a variable `$post_id` to the value of the first capture group in the URL, which is the post ID (assuming it's the first part of the filename, e.g., `post-123.html`).

Modified HTML Structure:

In each post's HTML file, you'll need to add a `link` element with the post ID as a parameter. For example, if your post HTML file is `post-123.html`, you can add the following link:
```html
<a href="/posts/{{ $post_id }}">Share or link to this post</a>
```
You can add this link anywhere in the post HTML file, such as at the top or bottom of the content.

Modifying the Existing HTML Files:

To add the link to all existing post HTML files, you'll need to iterate through the HTML directory and modify each file. You can do this using a tool like `find` and `sed`:
```bash
find /usr/share/nginx/html -type f -name "*.html" -exec sed -i 's/<\/body>/<a href="\/posts\/{{ $post_id }}">Share or link to this post<\/a><\/body>/' {} \;
```
This command finds all HTML files in the specified directory, replaces the last `</body>` tag with the desired link, and saves the changes.

Future Updates:

To ensure that future posts also have a link, you can add the link to your website's theme or template. For example, if you're using a template engine like Liquid, you can add the link to the template file.

